{"ref":"BDB, אַלִיַה","hw":"אַלִיַה","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אַלִיַה</span></big>  <strong>n.f. fat tail</strong> of sheep <strong>(</strong>Mish. <em>id.</em> 𝔗, <span dir=\"rtl\">אַלְיְתָה</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">אַלִּיתָא</span>, etc.; Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">أَلْيَة</span>, cf. Fl.<sup>TWB i. 418 a</sup><strong>)</strong> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 29:22\" href=\"/Exodus.29.22\">Ex 29:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 3:9\" href=\"/Leviticus.3.9\">Lv 3:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 7:3\" href=\"/Leviticus.7.3\">7:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 8:25\" href=\"/Leviticus.8.25\">8:25</a> (all ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">חֵ֫לֶב</span>); <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 9:19\" href=\"/Leviticus.9.19\">9:19</a>, prob. also <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 9:24\" href=\"/I_Samuel.9.24\">1 S 9:24</a> for <span dir=\"rtl\">הֶעָלֶיהָ</span> v. Gei Dr (cf. Tristram <sup>Nat. Hist. Bib. ch. vi</sup> Ri<sup>HWB Schafe</sup> Smith<sup>Dict. Bib. sheep</sup>).","next":"BDB, אִלּוּ","prev":"BDB, אֵלָה³"}